[{:db/id 17592186221420 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-047ba9d9-f028-5122-88f6-0f2794537abb" "question-2812ec6f-62e9-58a6-b999-e2e9bb1ef20a" "question-808ef5db-aeee-5e2b-ba0b-cf24a0046d0e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-047ba9d9-f028-5122-88f6-0f2794537abb" :question/id #uuid "047ba9d9-f028-5122-88f6-0f2794537abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-334280" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental matrix could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9da6b88c-3427-5d82-9c0a-0c12e0c3ee52"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9da6b88c-3427-5d82-9c0a-0c12e0c3ee52" :answer-field/id #uuid "9da6b88c-3427-5d82-9c0a-0c12e0c3ee52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-7eff2f7a-e7a9-5224-a158-a8a18a72ea74" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d6fa3d3b-1a20-5cf5-a0f8-b6beb40484d2" "answer-6aa1970d-083b-5e55-bd6c-f1afc347972b" "answer-7eff2f7a-e7a9-5224-a158-a8a18a72ea74" "answer-0b36848b-2da9-5c7b-a35d-1737517ad9ee" "answer-5ebdfe62-fb66-595a-82e4-7cd305075f0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6fa3d3b-1a20-5cf5-a0f8-b6beb40484d2" :answer/id #uuid "d6fa3d3b-1a20-5cf5-a0f8-b6beb40484d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6aa1970d-083b-5e55-bd6c-f1afc347972b" :answer/id #uuid "6aa1970d-083b-5e55-bd6c-f1afc347972b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7eff2f7a-e7a9-5224-a158-a8a18a72ea74" :answer/id #uuid "7eff2f7a-e7a9-5224-a158-a8a18a72ea74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b36848b-2da9-5c7b-a35d-1737517ad9ee" :answer/id #uuid "0b36848b-2da9-5c7b-a35d-1737517ad9ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{3t} & 2{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ebdfe62-fb66-595a-82e4-7cd305075f0e" :answer/id #uuid "5ebdfe62-fb66-595a-82e4-7cd305075f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3} & 2e \\\\ -2{e}^{3} & e\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2812ec6f-62e9-58a6-b999-e2e9bb1ef20a" :question/id #uuid "2812ec6f-62e9-58a6-b999-e2e9bb1ef20a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334287" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{t} \\\\ -{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 3{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{t} & {e}^{5t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & 3{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7e1c8270-c94c-5afb-bb4e-783c3deb13c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7e1c8270-c94c-5afb-bb4e-783c3deb13c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e1c8270-c94c-5afb-bb4e-783c3deb13c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-48b0a4b1-4b5e-5cdf-aad0-ef4cdc22aa18" :answer-field/choices ["answer-daaacd2a-601c-5c33-b2d1-7e81075a79a9" "answer-b9e625ba-41d6-5d24-be1f-0affef1526a6" "answer-eb7ccb52-fb72-55ec-b8fb-e2926647ecb3" "answer-48b0a4b1-4b5e-5cdf-aad0-ef4cdc22aa18" "answer-e6cecb96-8354-55c0-b574-aa891b5ab7fb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-daaacd2a-601c-5c33-b2d1-7e81075a79a9" :answer/id #uuid "daaacd2a-601c-5c33-b2d1-7e81075a79a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9e625ba-41d6-5d24-be1f-0affef1526a6" :answer/id #uuid "b9e625ba-41d6-5d24-be1f-0affef1526a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2e & {e}^{5} \\\\ -e & 3{e}^{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb7ccb52-fb72-55ec-b8fb-e2926647ecb3" :answer/id #uuid "eb7ccb52-fb72-55ec-b8fb-e2926647ecb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{t} & 3{e}^{5t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48b0a4b1-4b5e-5cdf-aad0-ef4cdc22aa18" :answer/id #uuid "48b0a4b1-4b5e-5cdf-aad0-ef4cdc22aa18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{t} & {e}^{5t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & 3{e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6cecb96-8354-55c0-b574-aa891b5ab7fb" :answer/id #uuid "e6cecb96-8354-55c0-b574-aa891b5ab7fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-808ef5db-aeee-5e2b-ba0b-cf24a0046d0e" :question/id #uuid "808ef5db-aeee-5e2b-ba0b-cf24a0046d0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-334308" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x,\\,{x}_{1}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{x}_{2}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs and two of its linearly independent solutions ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ shown above. Which of the following is a fundamental matrix for the system?" :question/worked-solution "Given a linear system ${x}^{′}=Ax,$ where $A$ is an $n\\times n$ matrix, a *fundamental matrix* $Φ(t)$ of the system is an $n\\times n$ matrix whose columns are linearly independent solutions of the system.\n\nIn our case, we have a $2\\times 2$ system. We are also given that the two linearly independent solutions of the system are the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}t+2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}=\\begin{bmatrix}(t+2){e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our fundamental could be written as\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & (t+2){e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Note:** The columns of $Φ$ can be written in any order." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8483fff-76a3-580a-a83e-5302b7c416d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8483fff-76a3-580a-a83e-5302b7c416d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8483fff-76a3-580a-a83e-5302b7c416d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a8593261-be32-5d9e-8dd8-02d165c8aae2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a2ea612-1a2e-591a-bff2-d4dd86480b2c" "answer-e765c34c-543a-5dd2-bfde-69ac7c6edaa3" "answer-673f5ad9-21c2-5daa-bb9e-6ee3d9dfe87f" "answer-b2aa5fbe-791f-52df-a6f5-eca385deaf15" "answer-a8593261-be32-5d9e-8dd8-02d165c8aae2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a2ea612-1a2e-591a-bff2-d4dd86480b2c" :answer/id #uuid "6a2ea612-1a2e-591a-bff2-d4dd86480b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}(t+2){e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e765c34c-543a-5dd2-bfde-69ac7c6edaa3" :answer/id #uuid "e765c34c-543a-5dd2-bfde-69ac7c6edaa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-673f5ad9-21c2-5daa-bb9e-6ee3d9dfe87f" :answer/id #uuid "673f5ad9-21c2-5daa-bb9e-6ee3d9dfe87f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & t+2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2aa5fbe-791f-52df-a6f5-eca385deaf15" :answer/id #uuid "b2aa5fbe-791f-52df-a6f5-eca385deaf15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-1} & 3{e}^{-1} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-1}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8593261-be32-5d9e-8dd8-02d165c8aae2" :answer/id #uuid "a8593261-be32-5d9e-8dd8-02d165c8aae2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & (t+2){e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-cedab975-3af3-5665-a2eb-98902cf38df0" :activity/id #uuid "cedab975-3af3-5665-a2eb-98902cf38df0" :activity/title "Fundamental Matrices" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050228 :activity/course 17592186046668 :activity/steps ["step-6298b8c6-ac0a-5b25-bb40-7c5832588d35" "step-eefffe20-3323-5fc2-a377-7246dd9a07f5" "step-7a388557-69a1-5e7f-9df1-7fa5c1163218"] :activity/first-step "step-6298b8c6-ac0a-5b25-bb40-7c5832588d35" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-6298b8c6-ac0a-5b25-bb40-7c5832588d35" :step/id #uuid "6298b8c6-ac0a-5b25-bb40-7c5832588d35" :step/content "question-047ba9d9-f028-5122-88f6-0f2794537abb" :step/next "step-eefffe20-3323-5fc2-a377-7246dd9a07f5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eefffe20-3323-5fc2-a377-7246dd9a07f5" :step/id #uuid "eefffe20-3323-5fc2-a377-7246dd9a07f5" :step/content "question-2812ec6f-62e9-58a6-b999-e2e9bb1ef20a" :step/next "step-7a388557-69a1-5e7f-9df1-7fa5c1163218" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7a388557-69a1-5e7f-9df1-7fa5c1163218" :step/id #uuid "7a388557-69a1-5e7f-9df1-7fa5c1163218" :step/content "question-808ef5db-aeee-5e2b-ba0b-cf24a0046d0e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133903 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-81171e25-e5ad-5118-af05-1058347bd84c" "question-ac0004d1-e33b-579f-a242-badcc09a2477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-81171e25-e5ad-5118-af05-1058347bd84c" :question/id #uuid "81171e25-e5ad-5118-af05-1058347bd84c" :question/math-academy-id "q-41477" :question/problem "![](images/29/296883eddf8dc4521e4fa1313e1f3176c965a376d55ecb9189fa913adc8d2625.png)\n\nPart of the graph of a function $y=f(x)$ with period $4$ is shown above. What is the graph of $y=f(x)$ on the interval $-6\\le x\\le 6?$" :question/worked-solution "The graph above shows the function in the interval $-2\\le x\\le 2.$\n\nSince this interval has length $4,$ and the period of the function is also $4,$ this interval represents a single period of the function.\n\nTherefore, the function will consist of many copies of the shape shown above, shifted horizontally by multiples of $4.$\n\n![](images/13/13eb143d92cd215f9283a44ad67ca91e679610d4b6625ae53ced56295430e843.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bbb74983-a5fb-5b54-80ff-62e42e368833"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bbb74983-a5fb-5b54-80ff-62e42e368833" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbb74983-a5fb-5b54-80ff-62e42e368833" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c7264fca-3bea-51fc-9e5c-4c009f2fe062" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7264fca-3bea-51fc-9e5c-4c009f2fe062" "answer-c9f360fa-fc4a-5b06-96ff-4de49594a49d" "answer-146ab018-a035-5b73-95a8-05742d6e5827" "answer-0638622e-b7c3-5da8-a7c5-6cb908cc9ef1" "answer-c5acf350-4f70-57a8-9daa-0cd77ef25e15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7264fca-3bea-51fc-9e5c-4c009f2fe062" :answer/id #uuid "c7264fca-3bea-51fc-9e5c-4c009f2fe062" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/13/13eb143d92cd215f9283a44ad67ca91e679610d4b6625ae53ced56295430e843.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9f360fa-fc4a-5b06-96ff-4de49594a49d" :answer/id #uuid "c9f360fa-fc4a-5b06-96ff-4de49594a49d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/19/192c95fa84b2a10e8131417d8aa8f27cfec426e304a8a5e5424eebf8b77f61cb.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-146ab018-a035-5b73-95a8-05742d6e5827" :answer/id #uuid "146ab018-a035-5b73-95a8-05742d6e5827" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/40/40e6d