-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$1.417$\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-6y+13) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}+{y}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-6y+13)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-6x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{y}^{2}-6) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-6x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{y}^{2}-6)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-{\\begin{bmatrix}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{n}}^{-1}{\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-{\\begin{bmatrix}6x-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6y\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{1}}^{-1}{\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}^{2}-6x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}-6\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{bmatrix}-{\\begin{bmatrix}6(2.25)-6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6(1.5)\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}3(2.25)^{2}-6(2.25) \\\\ 3(1.5)^{2}-6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{bmatrix}-{\\begin{bmatrix}7.5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}1.6875 \\\\ 0.75\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{7.5\\cdot 9-0\\cdot 0}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7.5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1.6875 \\\\ 0.75\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2.25 \\\\ 1.5\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{67.5}\\begin{bmatrix}15.1875 \\\\ 5.625\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ≈\\begin{bmatrix}2.025 \\\\ 1.417\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/id #uuid "d4e92ca9-095d-5013-a0f3-2a43f9ecb853" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer/id #uuid "ccb984f5-1d1e-5d3d-89ea-171fda9ca2b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.025" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204026 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" "question-ce47ce1b-5e64-5fb8-88b0-27f2349480f8" "question-d0e5e71c-da68-5727-a150-890764f120a1" "question-4033d90f-6820-5b6e-97e2-e268a68a992f" "question-5acc736b-d0d8-5439-9126-2975fad286b2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/id #uuid "e391a05d-f936-58b5-934a-ad5b4d40ee91" :question/math-academy-id "q-257213" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x,y)$ in the region $[0,1]\\times [-1,0]⊆{R}^{2},$ where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y.\n$$\n\nFill in the blanks in the matrix equation below that defines the first iteration of the Newton-Raphson process starting at the point $[1,\\,-1]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration. Round the answer for ${x}_{1}$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-5$\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$10$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-3}}</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-4}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-0.524$\n </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5x{y}^{2}-2xy-{x}^{2}+3y)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(5{y}^{2}-2y-2x) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(10xy-2x+3) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{y}^{2}-2y-2x) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(10xy-2x+3)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{\\begin{bmatrix}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 10y-2 \\\\ 10y-2 & 10x\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{\\begin{bmatrix}5{y}^{2}-2y-2x \\\\ 10xy-2x+3\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 10(-1)-2 \\\\ 10(-1)-2 & 10(1)\\end{bmatrix}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-\\begin{bmatrix}5(-1)^{2}-2(-1)-2(1) \\\\ 10(1)(-1)-2(1)+3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -12 \\\\ -12 & 10\\end{bmatrix}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get $({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})=\\begin{bmatrix}-29/82 \\\\ 39/82\\end{bmatrix}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{29}{82} \\\\ \\frac{39}{82}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{29}{82} \\\\ \\frac{39}{82}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ≈\\begin{bmatrix}0.646 \\\\ -0.524\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" "answer-field-85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" "answer-field-c7ba4597-ac27-5690-bf79-d5368cab1239" "answer-field-c3d09404-adf2-557f-9a06-f5a9863cc8b7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1efd346-8fdf-5f03-b6fe-b0884388016a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer/id #uuid "a610d803-1f33-5c3b-8170-83c03be1f7c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5feeab" :answer-field/id #uuid "85c0bc89-2005-520a-bca1-7bb0ed5