hson process starting at the point $[0,\\,1]^{T},$ and compute the components of the first iteration. Round the answer for ${x}_{1}$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$6$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})\\,=[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$-2$\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n$6$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">{{field-3}}</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{1}≈[$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\">$]$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "The Newton-Raphson method of optimizing a multivariable function $f:{R}^{n}\\to R$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-[{H}_{f}({x}_{n})]^{-1}∇f({x}_{n}),\n$$\n\nwhere $H({x}_{n})$ and $∇f({x}_{n})$ are the Hessian and gradient of $f$, respectively, evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nEquivalently, at each iteration, the above equation can be rewritten as\n\n$$\n{H}_{f}({x}_{n})({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-∇f({x}_{n}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6x{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-6xy+2x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6x{y}^{2}-3{x}^{2}-6xy+2x)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2 \\\\ 12xy-6x\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the Hessian is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}_{f}(x) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂x}(12xy-6x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂y}(6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2) & \\frac{∂}{∂y}(12xy-6x)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12y-6 \\\\ 12y-6 & 12x\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson system of equations is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12y-6 \\\\ 12y-6 & 12x\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{n}}({x}_{n+1}-{x}_{n})=-{\\begin{bmatrix}6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2 \\\\ 12xy-6x\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12y-6 \\\\ 12y-6 & 12x\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{0}}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-{\\begin{bmatrix}6{y}^{2}-6x-6y+2 \\\\ 12xy-6x\\end{bmatrix}}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12(1)-6 \\\\ 12(1)-6 & 12(0)\\end{bmatrix}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =-\\begin{bmatrix}6(1)^{2}-6(0)-6(1)+2 \\\\ 12(0)(1)-6(0)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}({x}_{1}-{x}_{0}) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system of equations, we get $({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1/3\\end{bmatrix}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ≈\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0.667\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4723ac7c-15e6-5105-8cff-0c025fd5d952" "answer-field-d1f5f30c-549c-5b34-abb8-940275af359d" "answer-field-bfb717c0-13de-5925-8e9a-3605309732dc" "answer-field-f29ded99-6e42-55a8-9e12-efe44e59e72b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4723ac7c-15e6-5105-8cff-0c025fd5d952" :answer-field/id #uuid "4723ac7c-15e6-5105-8cff-0c025fd5d952" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-00372683-1a17-5683-b8ec-944ce9ac2dae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-00372683-1a17-5683-b8ec-944ce9ac2dae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "